  <result type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">NUT-R5 Screening of under/malnutrition</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator aggregation-status="1" ascending="1" measure="1">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Number of people screened for under nutrition</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">1/ 2 Mobile Health and Nutrition Teams provide outreach  for  3 Health centers  2/  3 HC in Marolinta supported with RUTF, logistics, referral and training.
3/ Provision of CMAM   4/ OPD for children under 5 with SAM  5/ Promotion of improved IYCF practices for  children &lt; 2 years through CHW network.</narrative>
    </description>
    <reference code="NUT-I5" indicator-uri="https://dutchrelief.org/" vocabulary="99"></reference>
    <baseline iso-date="2021-12-21" value="0" year="2021">
     <dimension name="Age" value="Under 18"></dimension>
     <dimension name="Sex" value="Male"></dimension>
    </baseline>
    <baseline iso-date="2021-12-21" value="0" year="2021">
     <dimension name="Age" value="Under 18"></dimension>
     <dimension name="Sex" value="Female"></dimension>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2021-12-21"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2022-06-21"></period-end>
     <target value="1440">
      <dimension name="Age" value="Under 18"></dimension>
      <dimension name="Sex" value="Female"></dimension>
     </target>
     <actual value="1423">
      <dimension name="Age" value="Under 18"></dimension>
      <dimension name="Sex" value="Female"></dimension>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">ZOA/Medair screened 2759 children under 5 years for acute malnutrition through the mobile clinic sites and the Community Agent (CAs) network (97,14% of target achieved). Medair built community capacity through training and support to the CAs in the community, who provided active case finding, defaulter/absentee tracing and who promoted improved Infant and Young Child Feeding (IYCF) and household hygiene practices. A total of 100 CAs (M 52, F 48) and 5 (M 1, F 4) community supervisors were engaged and trained. 2794 mothers/caretakers were sensitized and trained for improved IYCF practices for children under 2 years. 2 MHNT provide outreach for 4 HC in Marolinta and Kopoky, instead of 3 HC targeted in Marolinta. The 4 HC are supported with RUTF, logistics, referral and training. In collaboration with the supported HC and following guidance of the Medicine Inspector of Beloha District, ZOA/Medair agreed to provide Expanded Program on Immunization (EPI) services to their beneficiaries. This increased EPI coverage amongst the children under 5 years. A total of 440 (M 204, F 236) children were vaccinated through the mobile clinic, while 2999 children were treated for IMCI Integrated Management of Childhood Illnesses.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
